# 8. CHALLENGES / ISSUES — MANG_03

This section must preserve the MANG_03 Issue architecture.

Do not reduce Issues to generic project risks, tickets, or task records.

Implement the following distinct concepts:

A. Issue Intake
B. Issue Qualification
C. Formal Issue Case
D. Issue–Solution Network
E. Impact Assessment
F. Issue Review
G. Decision and Escalation
H. Action Tracking
I. Outcome and Resolution

An initial submission is not automatically a formal Issue.

Implement a distinct Qualification Gate with the documented statuses:

- Ready.
- Information Needed.
- Duplicate.
- Out of Scope.
- Not Sure / Other.

Preserve the original submitted information.

Do not silently delete, merge, or rewrite an intake.

A qualified Issue enters the formal Issue–Solution process.

A duplicate must retain a traceable link to the relevant existing record.

Information Needed must retain the reason and missing information.

Out of Scope must retain its disposition rationale.

Do not silently discard an Issue because its classification is uncertain.

The system must support the MANG_03 principle that Issue qualification, urgency, priority, feasibility, and authority are separate concepts.

The initial Issue Intake must not require the submitter to calculate financial impact.

Financial and enterprise-level impact assessment belongs in the subsequent authorized managerial review.

Unknown and Not Assessed must remain explicit states.

