# 9. SOLUTIONS — MANG_03

Preserve the complete MANG_03 Solution model.

The system must distinguish:

1. Reusable Solution Type.
2. Case-specific Solution Candidate.
3. Candidate Assessment.
4. Candidate Feasibility.
5. Candidate Priority.
6. Candidate Decision.
7. Candidate Execution.
8. Candidate Outcome.

A reusable Solution Type is not the same as a case-specific Solution Candidate.

A Solution Candidate belongs to an Issue context.

The same Solution Type may produce different case-specific candidates under different conditions.

The same candidate must be capable of addressing multiple related Issues where the architecture supports it.

The Issue–Solution relationship is MANY-TO-MANY, CONDITIONAL, and EXTENSIBLE.

Do not implement a fixed linear Issue → Solution structure.

Do not force a misleading Solution Type when no suitable catalogue entry exists.

Preserve the documented MANG_03 MVP boundary around reusable catalogue authoring. Do not enable user-created reusable catalogue definitions simply because an interface button is convenient.

A case-specific Solution Candidate must still be recordable within the supported MVP rules.

Preserve the Solution assessment principles:

- Feasibility is separate from priority.
- Hard constraints are separate from weighted preferences.
- Financial impact is separate from profitability and cash-flow timing.
- A candidate ranking is not an authorization to decide.
- A selected candidate is not proof of success.
- A lower-level decision must not hide alternatives from higher-level authorized decision-makers.

Every candidate must retain its assumptions, evidence, conditions, constraints, assessments, and version history.

