# 20. REQUIRED END-TO-END ACCEPTANCE SCENARIO

The final application must support this complete scenario:

1. A user opens an existing Project.
2. The user identifies a material operational deviation.
3. The user submits an Issue Intake linked to the Project.
4. The system preserves the original submission and evidence.
5. The Issue passes through the Qualification Gate.
6. An authorized manager reviews and qualifies it.
7. The Issue becomes a formal Issue Case.
8. The Issue is linked to its affected Product, Project, Commitments, and relevant Resources.
9. The system displays relevant Solution Types.
10. Authorized users record case-specific Solution Candidates.
11. Each Candidate receives its own assessment.
12. Feasibility is evaluated independently of priority.
13. Shared-resource constraints and relevant opportunity costs are visible.
14. Decision Profiles can compare applicable alternatives.
15. A manager makes a decision within delegated authority or escalates.
16. Higher-level management can still see and reconsider all applicable alternatives.
17. The authorized decision creates one or more Actions.
18. Actions are assigned to responsible owners.
19. Progress and execution evidence are recorded.
20. Actual outcomes are independently reviewed.
21. Value preservation is recorded only when supported by evidence.
22. Lessons are captured and made available to future decision contexts.
23. The Home page and Value Map reflect the resulting verified changes.

At every stage, record provenance, identity, timestamps, and relevant history.

